# test.manifest: the image the guest suites boot to run the probes.
#
# The freestanding system call probes of build/tests at the root, the musl
# programs of build/tests/musl under /musl, the /etc the musl file and
# account probes read, and the name-resolution files the network probes
# read. A suite boots this image, runs probes and checks each one's success
# token. Host paths are relative to the repository root, where mkimage.sh
# runs.

exec-dir 0755 / build/tests

# The ISH shell, which `ishmusl` runs with -c and in its input mode to read
# the statuses it reports. It is the program os-simple stages as its login
# shell.
file 0755 /ish build/ish/ish
# musl's system(3) and popen(3) run /bin/sh -c, so the spawn probe needs a
# /bin/sh. ISH takes the -c form, and it is staged under both names, since
# KRFFS has no symbolic links.
dir 0755 /bin
file 0755 /bin/sh build/ish/ish
# A program for that shell to run, which the probe names by its full path:
# ISH has only `cd` and `exit` as builtins, so a command that prints has to
# be a program.
file 0755 /bin/echo build/utils/echo

# suidprobe's fixtures: the one helper program at several modes and owners.
# The exec-dir line above stages a plain 0755 /suidhelper, the control;
# these are the set-user-ID root copy suidprobe runs to become root, a
# set-user-ID copy owned by another account, whose identity the bit gives, a
# set-group-ID copy owned by another group, and a set-user-ID copy with no
# execute bit, which the execute check must refuse.
file 04755:0:0 /suidhelper.suid build/tests/suidhelper
file 04755:5:0 /suidhelper.u5   build/tests/suidhelper
file 02755:0:5 /suidhelper.sgid build/tests/suidhelper
file 04644:0:0 /suidhelper.nox  build/tests/suidhelper

# sudoprobe's fixtures: the reference sudo of utils/sudo.c, the answer to the
# coursework exercise, set-user-ID root, and a sudoers file that lists uid
# 1000. sudoprobe runs sudo as uid 1000 to become root, and as 1001 to be
# refused. No other image stages this program, since writing one is the
# exercise.
file 04755:0:0 /sudo build/utils/sbin/sudo
text 0644 /etc/sudoers # uids permitted to run sudo\n1000\n

# pwauthmusl's target: the set-user-ID root su of utils/su.c, the program and
# the mode os-simple stages, so the probe runs what a user runs. The probe's
# account is `probe` below, whose shell is the /idreport helper the exec-dir
# line stages, so a run of su reports the identity, the working directory,
# argv[0] and the environment it was given, and exits nonzero at the first
# that does not match. passwd, adduser, adduser-crash and login are the
# programs passwdmusl, addusermusl and loginmusl run.
file 04755:0:0 /su build/utils/sbin/su
file 04755:0:0 /passwd build/utils/sbin/passwd
file 0755:0:0 /adduser build/utils/sbin/adduser
file 0755:0:0 /adduser-crash build/utils/sbin/adduser-crash
file 0755:0:0 /login build/utils/sbin/login

# The probe account's home. It is a directory of its own and not the image's
# root, since a change to the directory the caller is in already would show
# nothing about a login su; the probe runs su from /musl and requires the
# login form to arrive here and the other form not to. It is 0700 and the
# account's, so entering it takes the target's privilege and not the
# caller's.
dir 0755 /home
dir 0700:1000:1000 /home/probe

# The sticky /tmp of the system images, where the musl probes make their
# files.
dir 1777 /tmp

# searchprobe's fixtures: a root-owned tree whose modes the probe changes to
# check that search permission is needed on every directory a path enters.
# The tree is staged, not made by the probe, because the execve cases need a
# program under the denied directory and a freestanding probe cannot write
# an ELF file; the directories that hold it are staged with it, and the
# probe checks these modes before it changes any. What the probe's cases
# change it makes and removes itself, so it finds this tree on every run.
# Every directory is 0777, because the probe denies by turning one of them
# into 0666: read and write stay granted, so only the missing execute bit
# can explain a refusal. /sp_denied/shared keeps its 0777 while /sp_denied is
# denied, so a refusal below it can only be the parent's search bit.
dir  0777 /sp_denied
dir  0777 /sp_denied/deep
dir  0777 /sp_denied/shared
text 0644 /sp_denied/leaf.txt one level down\n
text 0644 /sp_denied/deep/leaf.txt two levels down\n
file 0755 /sp_denied/prog build/tests/hello

# stickyprobe's pair: one sticky directory and one plain one, which differ in
# the one bit the probe tests, so that a denial in the first cannot come from
# the owner or a missing write bit. They are staged rather than made by the
# probe because `dir 1777` is how the system images' /tmp gets its bit, and
# nothing else reads that bit back, so the probe checks both modes before it
# does anything. What the probe's cases change, and the two other sticky
# directories its cases of a directory's owner and of the write check need,
# it makes and removes itself.
dir 1777 /st_sticky
dir 0777 /st_plain

dir 0755 /musl
exec-dir 0755 /musl build/tests/musl
# suidmusl's set-user-ID root copy: the plain 0755 /musl/suidmusl above is
# the parent, which changes to uid 1000 and runs this copy to check what the
# C library reports of a set-id exec: getresuid, getauxval(AT_SECURE) and the
# saved IDs.
file 04755:0:0 /musl/suidmusl.suid build/tests/musl/suidmusl
# Its execute-only copy, which uid 1000 may run and not read, so an exec of
# it must leave the process not dumpable.
file 0111:0:0 /musl/suidmusl.xonly build/tests/musl/suidmusl

# A small /etc: catfile reads motd and lists the directory, permmusl opens
# motd, and authmusl resolves root through passwd to uid 0. The shadow lines
# are fixed test credentials, committed, since the probes need known hashes
# to check. Root's password is "rach2" and probe's is "probepass", so that
# root's offered to `su probe` is a wrong password. The probe account is uid
# 1000 with /idreport as its shell and /home/probe as its home; /etc/group
# has the group of its gid.
dir 0755 /etc
text 0644 /etc/motd Welcome to Rach2 (test image).\n
text 0644 /etc/hostname rach2\n
text 0644 /etc/passwd root:x:0:0:root:/root:/bin/sh\nprobe:x:1000:1000:probe:/home/probe:/idreport\nprobe2:x:1001:1001:probe2:/home/probe:/idreport\n
text 0644 /etc/group root:x:0:\nprobe:x:1000:\nprobe2:x:1001:\n
text 0600 /etc/shadow root:$6$rach2test$br2Wb86wTtgiPWLN2WQoPqu69kGMNLnIQj3eaZLhG6sNTm9sN6ny.2af9tuaB/2HTw86.N3ZZN585IBoPgi0w/:0:0:99999:7:::\nprobe:$6$probetest$81REycl6dLv1SAkzSsuY0bx0yRoiYWOLkNshDgfNYybAChA02pRRKRGRlPADOnGg9SwQRz80cXN875vlU6LSF0:0:0:99999:7:::\nprobe2:$6$probe2test$v9NhhsuiXi4hOCF74Pbx1Wf6OFlAxvxA6U9pcCazHvodWv3lCg2LoShwjBUpyOazABVMnpgK2Ln2zNuIx2vpd0:0:0:99999:7:::\n

text 0644 /hello.txt hello, world\n
text 0644 /resolv.conf nameserver 10.0.2.3\n
text 0644 /hosts 127.0.0.1   localhost\n10.0.2.2    gateway\n10.0.2.3    dns\n10.0.2.15   rach2\n
